    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present design exposes untrusted public issue and repository content to broad shell execution, self-configuration, and GitHub push under full autonomy. The only declared preventive controls are prompt instructions, which earn one tier of behavioral credit and decay under model upgrade and longer task horizons. Forecast reaches critical because those prompt-based controls are the first to fail, and planned MCP expansion would add new egress risk. Manual validation was applied because scripts could not be run."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration artifacts provided, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No source code, tool schemas, MCP manifests, or runtime telemetry were provided, so capability details such as exact shell sandboxing, PR opening behavior, and audit logging are assessed from prompt and config only.",
    "Repository file contents were treated as untrusted because provenance and branch protections were not described; if the deployment limits issue-fixer to trusted branches only, some path confidence could change.",
    "The planned Slack MCP server is only described at a high level, so the forecast finding assumes a common outbound messaging deployment without pinned definitions or recipient binding."
  ]
